    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>forming&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;digit number,</p><p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#39;</mo><mtext>s</mtext></math>&nbsp;place</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi></math>,</p><p>So total number of ways will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;ways,</p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>forming&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;digit number when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#39;</mo><mtext>s</mtext></math>&nbsp;place&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi></math>,</p><p>So total number of ways will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;ways,</p><p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>forming&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;digit number,</p><p>So total number of ways will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math>&nbsp;ways,</p><p>Now adding all the cases we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>168</mn></math>&nbsp;ways.</p>"
